#20402
The Barrow Passage~
   A passage of fitted stone slabs leads into the mound, so low you must
stoop. The walls are carved with spirals, the ancient ones that the hill-
folk made long before the West ever used the sign. At the end lies an empty
stone bed, and claw marks on the ceiling above it.
~
