#20414
The Refectory~
   Long tables where monks and refugees eat together in silence: barley
bread, thin soup, water. The monks give their own portions to the children.
A reader stands at a lectern reading aloud the names of the dead buried in
the hills, one after another, as he has every day for forty years.
