#20416
The Library of the Dead~
   Shelves of scrolls and books record every barrow in the hills: who lies
in it, when they were buried, what rites keep them down. A monk at a desk is
copying one of them in great haste. He tells you without looking up that the
rites are failing, all of them, all at once.
~
